		{
			"id": "p31jYIPuuwwIJvLSh",
			"name": "Entrapment Area",
			"notes": "This spell makes a net or piece of fabric in the area of effect automatically fall on or wrap up a character.\nIf the subject enters the same hex as, or a hex adjacent to the fabric, it will attempt to grapple him. The victim must win a Contest of his DX (or his Wrestling skill), vs. the fabric's DX of 12. If the fabric wins the contest, it will entangle the victim for 1d-2 turns per hex of area covered by the fabric. For example, a rug that occupies 3 hexes would entangle the subject for 3d-6 turns.\nThis is also a Force spell.",
			"tags": [
				"Utility"
			],
			"vtt_notes": "This spell makes a net or piece of fabric in the area of effect automatically fall on or wrap up a character.\nIf the subject enters the same hex as, or a hex adjacent to the fabric, it will attempt to grapple him. The victim must win a Contest of his DX (or his Wrestling skill), vs. the fabric's DX of 12. If the fabric wins the contest, it will entangle the victim for 1d-2 turns per hex of area covered by the fabric. For example, a rug that occupies 3 hexes would entangle the subject for 3d-6 turns.\nThis is also a Force spell.",
